{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched — one node per agent, `command`/`role` as props. The `command` value is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND, run verbatim; a missing row, or a row without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly — nobody falls back to a machine default. Spawn shape: `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> -- <command>` (or the MCP equivalent). The rule nodes after the rows govern reviewing and choosing.","changed":"2026-08-26T20:09:42-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window, YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner at spawn: it must say Opus, not the machine default.\n\nTUI quirk: the composer's `❯` line shows PLACEHOLDER text (a suggestion or echo that was never typed) — it is NOT an unsent draft; never treat a populated-looking composer as pending human input. Applies to all Claude Code TUIs, fable included.","changed":"2026-08-26T20:09:56-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","concurrency":"HARD CAP: at most THREE concurrent Claude Opus AUTHOR lanes (daily-limit reasons); Opus REVIEWERS are exempt and do not count; grok/pi are outside the cap. The orchestrator queues further Opus work until a slot frees.","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix pins it everywhere (native on the API; a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — author and reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode. Reviews in a split of the author's worktree; proven author on infra-shaped and test-shaped work (its one UI authoring attempt was discarded — prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy).\n\nTUI quirk: a message sent while grok is mid-turn is QUEUED by default — after text → settle → Enter, if the screen shows the message queued rather than steering, press Enter once more.","changed":"2026-08-26T20:10:00-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"author+reviewer","usage-limit":"Do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low weekly-limit reading (the human can raise it); if a session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait.","watch-item":"Once spawned its OWN reviewer instead of reporting — reviewers are the orchestrator's to dispatch; authors report and stop. Watch for recurrence."}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. For design-first work only — the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author. Verify with the banner: it must say Fable.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:10:11-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"pi — author AND reviewer (kimi-k3 by default)","desc":"The pi CLI on its default model (kimi-k3). Author AND reviewer — proven at the complex end (closer to Opus-shaped than grok-shaped). Boots to a plain composer fast; the status bar's token counters are the working signal.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:10:10-04:00","custom":{"command":"pi","glitch-note":"kimi-k3 serving is the fragile part: known failure shapes are raw special-token emissions mid-tool-call (restart fresh in the same worktree with a resume pointer) and full-pool 429 outages. pi and opencode SHARE the Juspay kimi pool — they are not fallbacks for each other.","model":"kimi-k3 (pi's own default; no flag needed)","review-rule":"pi-authored PRs take BOTH grok AND Claude Opus as reviewers","role":"author+reviewer","watch-item":"Overruns role boundaries when the next step is obvious (has run suites as reviewer; once merged its own PR). Briefs for pi state the stop-lines explicitly; watch every lane."}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"opencode — reviewer (retired from the rotation)","desc":"Retired from the rotation; the row stands because historical lanes name it in `agent`/`reviewer` refs, and it can be seated on the human's word. opencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay — shares pi's pool and its outages). Quirks: has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review (brief it to title reviews with its tool name); its no-drift claims have been wrong before — weigh them accordingly.","changed":"2026-08-26T20:10:13-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode"}}
{"id":"roster-reviewer-contract","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a6","title":"The reviewer contract","desc":"A reviewer's job is READING THE CODE — the diff, the code around it, whether the PR body's claims hold, what breaks that nobody tested. Reviewers do NOT run test suites, ever; one surgical probe of ONE specific claim is allowed only where reading cannot settle it — never a suite, never e2e. Delivery: work in a split of the author's worktree, post ONE comment via gh (verdict + MUST/SHOULD/NIT at file:line), never edit/push/merge. Every review brief carries this contract in its header. An author never reviews its own lane. Reviewer pairing: grok or pi by default; pi-authored PRs take BOTH grok and Claude Opus.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:46-04:00"}
{"id":"roster-choosing","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a7","title":"Choosing an implementor","desc":"When the human didn't specify: claude-opus for complex, design-heavy, or cross-cutting work — the default. grok for infra-shaped and test-shaped work. pi is proven at the complex end — record wins and losses on its node. claude-fable is reserved for design-grade work. Flake lanes: pi or grok, never Opus.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:47-04:00"}
